Title: 0015-aros-system-menu-only
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0014-aros-system-window-border.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-16
Upstream-Status: local-only
Scope: AROS only, default of config.show_menubar in data/core/config.lua and the settings plugin.

Problem:
  With the system window border the editor showed two menus: the Intuition menu of the window and its own menu bar drawn inside the window.
Solution:
  Default config.show_menubar to false on AROS. The drawn bar can be switched on again from the system menu (View, Menu Bar) or in the settings.
Validation:
  2026-11-16, mainline nightly 20261113, AROS One 1.3 and Raspberry Pi nightly 20261110 in QEMU: the window shows no drawn menu bar at start.
Removal:
  Permanent for the AROS port.

diff --git a/data/core/config.lua b/data/core/config.lua
index 29e5875b..3260e97c 100644
--- a/data/core/config.lua
+++ b/data/core/config.lua
@@ -12,9 +12,10 @@ config.renderer = "default"
 
 ---Visibility of the responsive application menu bar.
 ---
----Defaults to true.
+---Defaults to true, except on AROS, where the commands are in the
+---system menu of the window.
 ---@type boolean
-config.show_menubar = true
+config.show_menubar = PLATFORM ~= "AROS"
 
 ---Keep the maximum FPS locked to current display refresh rate.
 ---
diff --git a/data/plugins/settings.lua b/data/plugins/settings.lua
index 8facdc6a..07ed7322 100644
--- a/data/plugins/settings.lua
+++ b/data/plugins/settings.lua
@@ -506,7 +506,7 @@ settings.add("User Interface",
       description = "Show the application menu bar on the top or inside the title bar in borderless mode.",
       path = "show_menubar",
       type = settings.type.TOGGLE,
-      default = true,
+      default = PLATFORM ~= "AROS",
       ---Apply saved or edited visibility through the bar's animated lifecycle.
       ---@param enabled boolean Whether the application menu bar should be shown
       on_apply = function(enabled)
